TECO DATA PROCESSING MACRO

; Initialize the environment
M $INIT
; Set up a buffer for data processing
$NEWBUF
; Define a sample input string (data)
G ^J
^J
; This is a comment in TECO macro context
; Process the data: Remove leading spaces
G ^J
^J
; Perform basic data validation (simple check)
; If the input is empty, exit gracefully
M $EXIT
; Output the result
$WRITE
; Clean up
$CLOSEBUF
$END

; NOTE: TECO commands are mixed with literal text.
; The above is a conceptual representation.
; In a real TECO macro file, you would see commands like
; ^A, ^B, ^C etc., and substitutions using ^X, ^Y etc.

; Example of a practical TECO data extraction snippet:
; Search for the first comma
S , R^A 1 ^Y
; Replace the first comma with a newline
S , ^R ^J
; Display the result
^X
